% Cold Therapy: LCD L33735 and its Policy Article A52460 (DME MACs). A policy
% program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery,
% benefit category, continued need, refills) and decides the claims for the
% codes the LCD and the Policy Article name — the fluid circulating cold pad
% with pump (E0218) and the reusable cold or hot bottles, ice caps, collars
% and wraps (A9273). The LCD states no coverage criterion: the one device it
% addresses "will be denied as not reasonable and necessary", and the
% reusable wraps have no criteria at all. So this policy CONCLUDES NOTHING:
% no claim it decides is reasonable and necessary, and a claim for its codes
% fails at the question. The codes are in scope, in the durable medical
% equipment benefit the Policy Article names ("Cold therapy devices are
% covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit"), and denied there.
%
% Not modelled: the non-DME cold therapy items the Policy Article sends to
% A9270 ("disposable single use fluid packs which generate cold temperature
% by a chemical reaction, devices in which ice water is put in a reservoir
% and then circulated through a pad by means of gravity or self-made
% containers used to administer cold therapy") — A9270 is the generic
% noncovered code, claimed by seat_lifts.le for the chair of a lift chair;
% the replacement pump of a water circulating pad (E0236), which the heating
% pads LCD L33784 names and heating_pads.le decides. Whether A9273 is within
% the benefit is not said by the cold therapy documents (the heating pads
% article A52502 says a nonelectric pad or wrap coded A9273 "does not meet
% the definition of durable medical equipment"): here it is in the benefit
% the Policy Article states for cold therapy devices, and not reasonable and
% necessary for want of any criterion.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base cold_therapy includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base cold_therapy includes:

LCD L33735 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33735".
the text of LCD L33735 is at "sources/lcd/L33735.txt".
Policy Article A52460 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52460".
the text of Policy Article A52460 is at "sources/article/A52460.txt".

section applicability is:

cold_therapy has no specific documentation requirements.

% The codes this policy decides: the cold pad with pump and the reusable
% cold or hot wraps; their benefit, durable medical equipment.
rule cold_therapy_codes with provenance Policy Article A52460,
        confer "Code E0218 describes a device which has an electric pump that circulates cold fluid through a pad":
the policy for code a code is cold_therapy
    if the code is in ["E0218", "A9273"].

rule cold_therapy_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52460,
        confer "Cold therapy devices are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is cold_therapy.

section question is:

% The LCD covers nothing: "A fluid circulating cold pad with pump (E0218)
% will be denied as not reasonable and necessary", and no criterion is
% stated for any other item. The rule below is this model's device for
% saying so: it concludes a claim reasonable and necessary only for a code
% in the list of the codes the LCD covers, which is empty — so that a claim
% fails at the question (the LCD's denial) and not for want of a rule.
rule cold_therapy_nothing_covered with provenance LCD L33735,
        confer "A fluid circulating cold pad with pump (E0218) will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the policy for code the code is cold_therapy
    and the code is in [].
